how do we tell a story movies can tell a  story with a spoken word the  screenwriter creates the scene and the  dialogue to accompany it movies can tell  a story with the images we see on screen  with expression and movement the actors  convey their inner thoughts and emotions  that bring deeper meaning to the spoken  words wow that sounds so much better  than omitting actors spend 90% of our  time pretending to be other people less  psychotic but  there's a reason going all the way back  to the days of silent films that there  was a pianist in the theater for it is  the musical score that can truly bring a  cinematic score to life  adding incredible power to the words we  hear in the visuals we see and when the  score is in the hands of an artistic  master like Lalo Schifrin a good film  a good film can become great and a great  film can be transformed into an all-time  classic it's been said of Lalo that his  work cannot be easily labeled I mean  it's what he creates jazz this is a  classical contemporary popular the  answer is yes  it is all of those things in whole or in  part for each film and that's because he  adapts his style to what filmmakers need  and doing so Lalo has called himself a  chameleon and I agree in the most  complimentary sense of what that means  for he is ever-changing  not hoping that the story fits his  musical style but being able as so few  can to make his musical score perfectly  match to the film and thus the story  gets told  try to imagine Dirty Harry without the  music that accompanies Harry's key  moments he's throwing his badge into the  river or the moment they find the girl  to me the music is heartbreaking it  conveys Harry's pain and yet it manages  like Clint himself to be cool cool  that's a pretty good word to describe a  composer whose music helped define the  music of the 60s from the Cincinnati kid  to Bullitt - Cool Hand Luke and all the  way through to the films of the past few  years and today including one of mine  the bridge of San Luis Rey his haunting  score honors Thornton Wilder's tribute  to love and I'm so pleased to be here to  thank you in person mr. schefren let's  be honest without the cool Mission  Impossible theme I'm betting Tom Cruise  fails in his mission the first time  which means no next five sequels Lalo is  so many things a true renaissance man a  performer at the piano a painter with  notes a conductor and composer who has  scored some of the most memorable films  of the past half century let's take a  look and listen to the man and his work
 

